From ff30c367e812c4a80afbed17096342ade76f5856 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini engine authoring <engine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:55:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 112/113] Reuse the light object list of the object update in
 the light manager

The light manager walked every object of the scene to find the lights
several times per update (enabled test, light count, light copy and the
background light test); with hundreds of thousands of instances that is
the larger part of a light edit. The object manager now collects the light
objects in object order while it assigns object indices, and the light
manager uses that list. The list is invalidated whenever the object
manager is tagged (objects added, removed or modified, including a change
of geometry), so the light manager, which runs after the object update of
a scene update, always reads a fresh list; a caller before the object
update (the background light test of the shader manager) then walks the
objects as before.

CYCLES_FULL_LIGHT_WALK walks every object as before, as a reference.
CYCLES_VERIFY_LIGHT_LIST compares the list used with walking every object
on every light manager update and reports a difference as an error.

Rationale: On large instanced scenes each light edit walked all objects four times in the light manager, about 10-20 ms per edit on 380k objects.
Contract: The light objects used, and their order, are those found by walking every object (checked by CYCLES_VERIFY_LIGHT_LIST); kernel lights, light tree and distribution are unchanged.
Tests: tests/houdini_light_list_smoke.py
